  receipts: [
    "**In v2 infer, the result of a call whose callee returns a DECLARED (non-kernel) type is judged where it is used (climbed, sunny-wolf-624).** Re-measured on main 1f25232cdc through the production assembly route with a std.nat peer (v2.test.claim.compiler.declared_return_result): `fn mk() -> Nat { 0 }` used at `fn f() -> Bool { mk() }` REFUSES `arrow_body_does_not_inhabit_declared_return`; the generic `fn mk<T>(xs: List<T>) -> Nat` counterpart refuses the same; `wants_bool(mk())` refuses `application_argument_does_not_inhabit`; an instantiated generic coproduct `Out<Int>` at Bool refuses the declared-return reason; `fn f() -> Nat { mk() }` is accepted. The kernel Int-at-Bool control refuses the same declared-return reason. The original filing (session/stern-swift-290-literal) had Nat-at-Bool ACCEPTED; #13325's `infer_application_result_type` plus later main is what closed the specimens. Deleting drr_declared_return_call_results_are_judged must make a control fail.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS, AS FILED (now closed on the production route). The kernel/declared split was the discriminator: kernel Int was judged and a declared Nat was not. Independent of generics. Distinct from comparison_operands_never_judged_in_v2_infer. XL-2's collection size row still states Int until BOTH this class (now judged) AND literal elaboration at Nat hold -- see gunbc.rung_drop collection_count_result_stated_int_until_declared_results_are_judged.",

    "N7 RELEVANCE (calm-boar-904 asked). NOT N7's current wall: all 8 N7 tests (//v2/test/parse/expression_bodied_fn_decl_parse:all) stop at infer_reason_projection_receiver_declaration_unavailable on `root.children` in g_tree_has_arrow_body, whose receiver is a PARAMETER declared Node -- its declaration is unavailable because v2.std.node itself fails to resolve (the chain's preceding resolve link is a bare `count` in v2.std.node, the collection-size wall gunbc#13307 addresses). LIKELY THE NEXT ONE: the same test reads `artifact.tree` off a match binder of parse_module_prepared's result, a callee returning the declared Outcome<ParseArtifact>; once v2.std.node resolves, that projection's receiver is a declaration-typed call result -- this class -- and is expected to be where the chain stops next. To be confirmed by the N7 re-measure after #13307 lands.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: mechanically preventable (enrolled production-route REDs in v2.test.claim.compiler.declared_return_result). CEILING: structurally guaranteed. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: the compiler derives a proof or refusal from modeled structure so a call whose callee declares a non-kernel return cannot be an Accepted program with an unjudged result -- SUFFICIENT FOR deleting the inhabitance claims' production machinery while keeping the REDs enrolled. Residual: infer_reference_facts_or_frontier still rewrites a Rejected Arrow grounding to GroundingNotDerived; that concealment is not the Nat/Out specimens (they refuse), and must not silently accept.",
